A temperature and humidity sensor is an electronic device that measures the ambient temperature and relative humidity of the surrounding environment. These sensors are widely used in weather stations, home automation systems, greenhouses, industrial applications, and IoT (Internet of Things) projects.

🧊 Temperature Sensor
Measures the heat or thermal energy in the environment.

Units: Usually measured in Celsius (°C) or Fahrenheit (°F).

Common types: Thermistor, RTD, thermocouple, and semiconductor-based sensors.

💧 Humidity Sensor
Measures the amount of water vapor in the air.

Expressed as Relative Humidity (RH%), which indicates the percentage of moisture in the air compared to the maximum it can hold at a given temperature.

🔧 Common Combined Sensor Modules:
These modules often combine both temperature and humidity sensors in one device:

DHT11: Basic and low-cost; slower and less accurate.

DHT22 (AM2302): More accurate and wider range than DHT11.

SHT31: Higher precision and reliability.

BME280: Also includes pressure sensing.

📦 Typical Uses:
Weather monitoring systems

Smart home HVAC control

Greenhouse environmental control

Data logging and IoT applications


